  "page_gates": "NO GRAIN CONFLICT - THIS IS THE FIRST FILING OF THE CYCLE. The cover fills Current Report AND Cumulative Totals with the SAME figures (contrib 9,768.17 / exp 8,828.72 / balance 939.45) and leaves Last Report empty, so period and cumulative are the same number by construction and the ledger cannot be ambiguous between them. CONTRIBUTIONS gated by the schedule's own printed 'Total Contributions: $9768.17' at the head of p2: the 49 rows over pp2-3 sum to 9,768.17 EXACTLY, and to the cover. EXPENDITURES gated by p4's own printed 'Total amount of expenditures: $8828.72': the 19 rows sum to 8,828.72 EXACTLY, and to the cover. Campaign-balance cross-check, a third independent gate: 9,768.17 - 8,828.72 = 939.45, which is the cover's stated balance to the cent. ROW-COUNT GATE: rowbands found 59 bands on p2, 55 on p3, 25 on p4; the ledger rows occupy the odd bands 11-59 on p2 (25 rows), bands 2..49 on p3 (24 rows) and bands 3-21 on p4 (19 rows), and 25+24 = 49 contribution rows and 19 expense rows are what was read - no band holding text is unaccounted for. GEOMETRY SPOT-CHECKS (4, all reproduced): p2 band 15 -> '2/4/20 / Malena Stevens / 50'; p3 band 2 -> '5/25/20 / James Simone / 105.47'; p3 band 49 -> '6/21/20 / Kara Smith / 50'; p4 band 21 -> '6/22/20 / Park Record / Campaign Ad / 561'. FIELD-SHIFT SCREEN: passed - both sheets print their own column headers (Date | Name of Contributor | Mailing Address | Zipcode | Amount, and Date | Person or Organization | Purpose of Expenditure | Amount), the detected vertical rules match those headers, and every wrapped address stays inside its own band.",
