  "notes": "Malena Stevens, County Council, 2020 PRIMARY - the first of her three 2020 filings and the anchor of the chunk's cover-differencing chain. Clean typed sheets (born-digital laser print, scanned) with a usable county OCR layer; nothing handwritten, no redactions, no specimen rows, no struck values.\n\nA SOURCE PROPERTY THIS BRIEF DOES NOT LIST, AND IT REVERSES A WAVE PRECEDENT ON THIS FILING. The brief records, from the McKenna 2024 pair, that 'IN-KIND is a separate schedule with its own printed total, and the cover's contribution figure is MONETARY-ONLY'. That is NOT true here. Stevens carries her two in-kind items INLINE in the main ledgers - 1/24/20 Malena Stevens $160 'Website & Design' and 1/28/20 Ghent Bailey $50 'Logo Design' - each annotated '(In Kind)' in the amount cell, each entered TWICE (once as a contribution, once as the matching expenditure, the classic in-kind double entry), and each INCLUDED in the schedule's own printed total. The arithmetic proves it and leaves no room for a judgement call: monetary-only the contributions come to 9,558.17 and the expenses to 8,618.72, and only WITH the $210.00 do they reach the printed 9,768.17 and 8,828.72 that both the schedules and the cover state. Flagging these four rows in_kind would therefore have made build_finance publish an itemized sum 210.00 short of a cover it actually matches to the cent - a fabricated discrepancy on a filing that reconciles perfectly. They are shipped as ordinary rows with in_kind=false and the '(In Kind)' annotation preserved verbatim in each row note. THE PRECEDENT TO CARRY FORWARD IS THEREFORE NARROWER THAN THE BRIEF STATES: whether in-kind sits inside or outside the stated total is a PER-FILER convention that must be settled by the page's own arithmetic on every filing, never assumed from the 2024 pair.\n\nONE BAD DATE, NOT REPAIRED: expense line 4 prints '2/30/20', an impossible day. Blanked with needs_review=1 and the verbatim kept in the row note.\n\nCOVER-DIFFERENCING (recorded because the CHUNK_BRIEF asks for it): the Stevens 2020 trio is Primary 11110 (this filing), Pre-Election 11861 and Post-Election 12943 (another agent's, already recorded). 12943's cover states last_report contrib 10,157.17 / exp 9,217.72, which is what 11861 must state as its cumulative; differencing THIS filing against that gives a pre-election period of exactly 389.00 on BOTH sides (10,157.17 - 9,768.17 = 389.00 and 9,217.72 - 8,828.72 = 389.00). That prediction was made from this record before 11861 was opened and is used there as an external gate. Note also that 12943 is period-scoped on both sides and was withheld for it, whereas this Primary filing has no period/cumulative gap at all - the grain question is not a property of the county's form but of where a filing sits in its cycle."
